  "raw_text": "102\n\nKauhla piua\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncold weather season\n \n/ temporada de clima frío\n\nKauhla wahwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto suffer from cold\n \n/ sufrir de frío\n\nLî kauhla\n \n–\n \ncold water\n \n/ agua fría\n\nKaupin\n \n(\ndb,lv\n; not in / no en:\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nfence, wall, fence or wall around a garden or vineyard, garden\n \n/ cerca,\nmuralla, muro, cerca o muro alrededor de un jardín o viñedo, jardín\n\nKayu\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsugar\n-\ncane\n \n/ caña de azúcar\n\nKek\n \n(\ndict,dictu\n;\n \nKik\n-\ndb,dba,dictu-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncake\n \n/ pastel\n\nKi\n \n–\n \nAt end of a question, this particle tells the listener that the sentence is a question. It can be compared to the way a\n\nperson’s pitch is raised at the end\n \nof a question. / Al final de una pregunta, esta partícula le dice al oyente que la\noración es una pregunta.\n \nSe puede comparar con la forma en que se eleva el tono de una persona al final de una\n\npregunta.\n\nRait ki?\n \n–\n \nReally?\n \n/ ¿De verdad?, ¿De\n \nveras?,\n \n¿\nEn serio?\n\nKî\n \n(Ki)\n \n(1) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nisland, key\n \n/ isla, cayo\n\n(Construct:\n \nKîka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nPatmos kîka\n \n–\n \nisland of Patmos\n \n/ isla de Patmos)\n\nKî dakura\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nisland\n \n/ isla\n\nKî\n \n(Ki)\n \n(2) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nkey, lock, padlock\n \n/ llave, cerradura, candado\n\n(Construct:\n \nKîka\n)\n\nKî mihta\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nkey (for a lock)\n \n/ llave (para una cerradura)\n\nKîa\n \n(Kia)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfragrance, scent, smell, odor\n \n/ fragancia, aroma, olor\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb\n):\n \nsîka maka kîa painkira\n \n–\n \nperfumed incense\n \n/ incienso perfumado)\n\nKîa briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto smell\n \n/ oler\n\nKîa pain angkaia ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nincense\n \n/ incienso\n \n(Alt:\n \nIsintka\n;\n \nKîa pain batanka sunukira ba\n)\n\nKiasma kîa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsmell of smoke\n \n/ olor a humo\n\nKiawalaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKyawalaia\n,\n \nKia walaia\n,\n \nKîa walaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto kiss, to smell\n \n/ besar, oler\n\nKiabits\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncabbage\n \n/ repollo\n\nKiaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKyaya\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nthorn, prickle, bramble, fish bone, spine\n \n/ espina, zarza, espina de pescado, columna vertebral\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb90\n):\n \nkiaya kraunka kum\n \n–\n \na crown of thorns\n \n/ una corona de espinas\n)\n\nKyaya dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbush\n \n/ arbusto\n\nSikiski kiaikira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhedgehog\n \n/ erizo\n\nKiama\n \n(a/t:\n \nKyama\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \near, ears\n \n/ oreja, oregas, oído\n\n(Construct:\n \nKiaima\n \n–\n \nmy ear\n \n/ mi oreja;\n \nKiamam\n \n–\n \nyour ear\n \n/ tu oreja;\n \nAi kiama\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their ear\n \n/ su oreja)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb88\n):\n \nPita ispara kum saki Malco kiama ba klakan\n \n–\n \nPeter, taking out a sword, cut off Malchus’ ear\n \n/ Pedro, sacando una\n\nespada,\n \ncortó la oreja de Malco\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nhf\n-\n7\n):\n \nkiama pri tniki wals\n \n–\n \ngive\n \nundivided attention\n \n/ prestar toda la atención\n \n(\nLit\n:\n \nlisten (with your) ear free and leaning\n \n/\n\nescucha (con tu) oreja libre e inclinada\n)\n\nKiama karna\n \n–\n \nunheeding, not listening, obstinate, stubborn\n \n/ sin escuchar, obstinado, terco\n\n(Lit:\n \nhard ear\n \n/ oreja dura\n)\n\nKiama lihngni\n \n(\ndict\n;\n \nK\ni\nama lihni\n-\ndb,\ndictu\n-\nalt\n;\n \nK\ni\nama li\nng\nni\n-\ndictu\n;\n \nK\ny\nama lihni\n-\nlv\n)\n \n–\n \nattentive, obedient, submissive\n\n/ atento, obediente,\n \nsumiso\n\nKiama lula\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nearring\n \n/ arete\n\nKiamapara\n \n(\nd\nb,km,sjj,jw\n);\n \na/t\n:\n \nKiama para\n-\ndict\n,\ndictu\n;\n \nKyama para\n;\n \nKyamapara\n-\nbh,lv\n)\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \nrebellious,\n\ndisobedient\n, rebellious person, disobedient person\n \n/ rebelde, desobediente, persona rebelde, persona\n\ndesobediente\n\nKiama prawan\n \n–\n \ndeaf\n \n/ sordo\n\n(Lit:\n \near closed\n \n/ oreja cerrada\n)\n\nKiamda\n \n(\ndb,fy,km,my,bm,dictu\n;\n \nKiamdar\n-\ndict\n;\n \nKarpenter\n,\nKarpinter\n-\ndictu\n;\n \nKiamda\n,\nKarpinta\n-\nmwb\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncarpenter\n \n/\n\ncarpintero\n\nKiamil\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nKyamil\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncamel\n \n/ camello\n\nKiamka\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nKyamka\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndescendant, breed, clan\n, race, tribe, family, offspring, relative\n \n/ descendiente, raza, clan,\n\ntribu, familia, descendencia, pariente\n\n(Construct:\n \nKiamki\n;\n \nKiamkam\n;\n \nAi kiamka\n)",
